  "id": "acid-drift",
  "name": "Acid Drift",
  "tagline": "Wind that moves with a single-note acid line.",
  "description": "Wind that rises and falls with the acid line's slow filter sweep. A single-note acid line; offbeat ticks; a steady kick; open hats now and then. The build is long and its tides come slowly.",
  "use": {
    "name": "Flow",
    "for": "Long, absorbed stretches on a single task.",
    "why": "A hypnotic line that holds one note while its timbre moves over minutes. That is slow, continuous novelty, which resists habituation over long sessions without ever becoming an event. The wind follows the acid's sweep, so the ambience and the music move as one."
  },
